<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21068] sanityn test_81d: client OOM forking 10000 mrename processes</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21068</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanityn test_81d (parallel rename file cross-dir, added by &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17426" title="parallel cross-directory rename of regular files on single MDT" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17426"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17426&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;) starts one background mrename per file with no throttle: MDSCOUNT * COUNT = 10000 processes with the default COUNT=2500 and 4 MDTs, then waits for them all.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On a 3GB aarch64 client with 16KB PAGE_SIZE (rocky10 6.12.0-211.47.1.el10_2) the test was OOM-killed in about 1/3 of runs. At the OOM about 5700 mrename processes were alive: page tables used 650MB (16KB pages make each minimal process's page tables ~4x larger than with 4KB pages) plus 94MB of kernel stacks and transient COW copies of the forked test shell. Lustre page cache was ~2MB, so this is the test, not the filesystem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Out of memory: Killed process 536825 (bash) total-vm:17264kB, anon-rss:12992kB, ... pgtables:128kB
 sanityn test_81d: @@@@@@ FAIL: not crossdir: 9998 != 10000
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: limit the number of concurrent mrename processes, while still renaming from both mounts and all MDTs at the same time.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
